                    "text": "in 2 \"external clock (phasor)\""
                }
            },
            {
                "box": {
                    "code": "/**\n * ============================================================================\n * @file offset-spline-random.gendsp / offset-spline-random.maxpat\n * @title OFFSET-SPLINE-RANDOM (Continuous Drunk Walk with 6-Point Hermite Spline)\n * @author Max Bruckert (assisted by Gemini)\n *\n * @description\n * Smooth random walk modulation source. Uses 6-point cubic spline interpolation\n * across sampled random walk steps to generate fluid, natural, organic control\n * voltages without discrete stair-stepping or zipper noise. Supports internal\n * phasor drive or external audio-rate trigger sampling.\n *\n * @inlets\n *   in1 : Audio / Signal Thru (Optional Carrier / Mix)\n *   in2 : External Clock Trigger (Sample trigger when trigmode = 1)\n *\n * @outlets\n *   out1 : Folded Audio Output (mixed input + scaled random walk)\n *   out2 : Step Trigger Impulse\n *   out3 : Smooth Spline Interpolated Random Walk CV\n *   out4 : Stepped Sample & Hold Random Walk CV\n *\n * @parameters\n *   amp       (0..1, def: 0.2)       : Output attenuation level\n *   trigmode  (0..1, def: 0)         : Clock source (0 = Internal phasor, 1 = External in2)\n *   frequency (0.01..500 Hz, def: 20): Internal trigger generator frequency\n *   range     (0..100, def: 50)      : Random walk step deviation intensity\n *   mode      (0..1, def: 1)         : Interpolation mode (0 = stepped S&H, 1 = smooth spline)\n * ============================================================================\n */\nParam amp(0.2, max=1, min=0);\nParam trigmode(0, max=1, default=0, min=0);\nParam frequency(20, min=0.01, max=500);\nParam range(50, max=100, min=0);\nParam mode(1, max=1, default=1, min=0);\n\n// --- D\u00e9clarations des m\u00e9moires ---\nDelay delay_fb(120);            // D\u00e9lai pour le feedback du mixage\nHistory h_phase(0);             // M\u00e9moire de la phase pr\u00e9c\u00e9dente\nHistory h_rand_walk(0);         // Accumulateur pour la marche al\u00e9atoire\nHistory p0(0), p1(0), p2(0), p3(0), p4(0), p5(0); // Registres \u00e0 d\u00e9calage pour spline\n\n// --- 1. Gestion du Trigger & Phase ---\n// S\u00e9lection entre le phasor interne et le signal d'entr\u00e9e 2\nphasor_int = phasor(frequency, 0);\nphase = trigmode ? in2 : phasor_int;\n\n// D\u00e9tection du front (trigger) : vrai quand la phase red\u00e9marre ou saute brusquement\n// On utilise delta() pour d\u00e9tecter un changement significatif (ex: passage de 0.9 \u00e0 0.1)\ntrig = abs(delta(phase)) > 0.5;\n\n// --- 2. G\u00e9n\u00e9ration du Bruit (Box-Muller transform pour bruit Gaussien) ---\nn1 = noise();\nn2 = noise();\nu1 = abs(n1);\nu2 = n2 * PI;\n// G\u00e9n\u00e9ration de la composante al\u00e9atoire\ngen_noise = sqrt(log(max(u1, 0.000001)) * -2.0) * cos(u2); \n\n// --- 3. Marche Al\u00e9atoire & Registre \u00e0 d\u00e9calage ---\n// On met \u00e0 l'\u00e9chelle le bruit et on l'ajoute \u00e0 la position pr\u00e9c\u00e9dente\nscale_amt = scale(range, 0, 100, 0, 4);\nstep = gen_noise * scale_amt;\nh_rand_walk = fold(h_rand_walk + (trig ? step : 0), -1, 1);\n\n// Mise \u00e0 jour du registre \u00e0 d\u00e9calage lors d'un trigger (Bucket Brigade)\nif (trig) {\n    p5 = p4;\n    p4 = p3;\n    p3 = p2;\n    p2 = p1;\n    p1 = p0;\n    p0 = h_rand_walk;\n}\n\n// --- 4. Interpolation Spline ---\n// G\u00e9n\u00e8re une courbe douce entre les 6 derniers points stock\u00e9s\nsig_spline = interp(phase, p5, p4, p3, p2, p1, p0, mode=\"spline6\");\nsig_stepped = p0; // Signal par paliers (non liss\u00e9)\n\n// --- 5. Mixage & Sorties ---\nsig_final = mode ? sig_spline : sig_stepped;\naudio_out = fixdenorm(sig_final * amp);\n\n// Input signal processing (Subtle feedback loop)\ntap_fb = delay_fb.read(120);\nmixed_input = mix(in1, tap_fb, 0.5);\ndelay_fb.write(mixed_input);\n\n// Sortie finale : m\u00e9lange de l'entr\u00e9e et du bruit g\u00e9n\u00e9r\u00e9\nout1 = fold(mixed_input + audio_out, -1, 1);\n\n// Sorties utilitaires\nout2 = trig;        // Signal de trigger\nout3 = sig_spline;  // Spline smoothing monitor\nout4 = sig_stepped; // Visualisation des paliers",
                    "fontface": 0,
                    "fontname": "<Monospaced>",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-3",
                    "maxclass": "codebox",
